# Line endings, for a harness that runs on three platforms.
#
# The golden gates compare bytes: a fixture against a capture, a generated
# artifact against the committed one, a manifest against the manifest a build
# actually wrote. Git's default on Windows is to rewrite line endings on
# checkout, which would turn every one of those comparisons into a diff of
# invisible characters. So the working tree is LF everywhere, on every
# platform, and the files that are data rather than text are never touched at
# all.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The captured fixtures are data. They were extracted from bundles the
# reference implementation wrote, and nothing may transform them between the
# capture and the comparison -- not an editor, not a checkout.
golden/fixtures/**              -text
golden/analysis/vectors/*.json  -text
golden/analysis/plans/*.json    -text
golden/analysis/plans/contract.json -text
golden/parity/FIXTURES.json     -text
golden/parity/**/tour.json      -text

# The parity pictures are photographs, compared pixel for pixel against a
# fresh walk's own. A checkout that touched one would be a difference nobody
# introduced, on the one gate whose whole point is that no count can see it.
golden/parity/screens/**/*.png  binary

# Bundles are zip archives. None is committed today; if one ever is, it is
# bytes.
*.atlas binary
